message.content:
I found two possible lesions, both on the lower jaw. I'm not confident in either.

```json
{"lesions": [
  {"box": [0.642, 0.666, 0.671, 0.728], "pai": 3},
  {"box": [0.454, 0.611, 0.495, 0.673], "pai": 3}
]}
```

1. **Lower left premolar, at the root tip** (about pixels 1570–1640 × 860–940 in the 2444×1292 image). The bone around the root tip is darker and has lost some density, with a small dark spot just below it. The outline isn't clearly defined, so I graded it 3. If you read the border as well defined, it would be a 4.
2. **Lower right incisor/canine, at the root tip** (about pixels 1110–1210 × 790–870). There's a broad, faint dark area around the root tip. Panoramic images often look dark at the centre front of the lower jaw because of the airway and tongue overlapping, so this one could be an artifact rather than a lesion. That makes it the less certain of the two.

I didn't find any clear lesions on the upper teeth or the lower molars. I found these by enhancing the contrast of crops of the image and looking at them. This is an image-based estimate, not a clinical diagnosis.
